Package: claude-usage
Version: 0.11.22
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), python3-cairo, python3-pil, systemd
Recommends: gnome-shell (>= 45) | plasma-workspace, google-chrome-stable | chromium-browser
Description: Claude.ai usage indicator for GNOME and KDE Plasma
 Shows Claude.ai weekly usage percentage in the GNOME top panel and dock, or
 in the KDE Plasma panel.
 .
 GNOME: a two-ring dock icon (All models outer ring, Sonnet only inner ring),
 a color-coded panel label with scroll-wheel toggle between metrics, and
 user-configurable ring colors via a GNOME preferences UI. KDE: a native
 Plasma 6 plasmoid with the same rings, colors, and pacing popup, configured
 via the widget's settings. The active desktop loads whichever applies; the
 package ships both plus the shared local server.
 .
 Data is fetched every 7 minutes by the Claude Usage Tracker Chrome
 extension, which reads your existing Claude.ai session — no API keys or
 stored credentials required.
 .
 After installing this package, run: claude-usage-setup
